{"title":"Banyan Language Schools","sub":"Where will the value come from?","type":"Private equity","industry":"Education","geo":"Vietnam","diff":3,"fmt":"Candidate-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Private equity value creation · operating leverage · EBITDA bridge","prompt":"A PE fund is buying Banyan, which runs 40 English-language schools for children in Vietnam. The price is 9× EBITDA, with debt of 4× EBITDA. The partner asks you to build the value-creation plan: how much could EBITDA grow in five years, from which levers, and what return would that give?","clarify":[{"q":"School economics?","a":"Each school has 600 places and is 70% full. Families pay $3,000 a year. Teaching materials and part-time tutors cost $600 per student; rent and core staff $700k per school a year."},{"q":"Levers?","a":"Management believes better marketing and timetabling can fill schools to 80%, fees can rise 5% with new digital homework tools, and 10 new schools can open in under-served cities."},{"q":"New schools?","a":"Each costs about $2M to open, paid from cash flow, and within three years reaches the same economics as an existing school after the improvements (80% full, fees 5% higher)."},{"q":"Debt at exit?","a":"About $30M."}],"structure":{"root":"How much value can the fund create at Banyan?","branches":[{"head":"Fill existing schools","items":["Utilisation 70% → 80%"]},{"head":"Charge more","items":["Fees +5%"]},{"head":"Open new schools","items":["10 schools","Capital needed"]},{"head":"Returns","items":["Exit value − debt vs equity in"]}]},"hypothesis":"Schools have high fixed costs, so each extra student is very profitable. I expect filling empty seats to be the biggest lever.","questions":[{"q":"What does one school earn today, and what is Banyan's EBITDA?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Students: 600 × 70% = 420. Each contributes $3,000 − $600 = $2,400: $1,008k. Less $700k fixed: <b>$308k</b> per school.</p> <p>Across 40 schools: <b>$12.3M</b> EBITDA.</p>"},{"q":"Build the EBITDA bridge to year 5.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"378.16pt\" height=\"195.16pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 378.16 195.16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 195.16 L 378.16 195.16 L 378.16 0 L 0 0 L 0 195.16 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 25 160.16 L 370.96 160.16 L 370.96 10.472 L 25 10.472 L 25 160.16 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"ma99844d2ee\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#ma99844d2ee\" x=\"61.236917\" y=\"160.16\" style=\"fill: #4a5568; stroke: #4a5568; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #4a5568\" transform=\"translate(36.230042 175.36) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-22\" d=\"M 3322 0 L 595 0 L 595 4467 L 3322 4467 L 3322 3994 L 1133 3994 L 1133 2496 L 3194 2496 L 3194 2022 L 1133 2022 L 1133 474 L 3322 474 L 3322 0 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-1f\" d=\"M 595 0 L 595 4467 L 2432 4467 Q 2982 4467 3302 4153 Q 3622 3840 3622 3315 Q 3622 2982 3504 2784 Q 3386 2586 3216 2490 Q 3046 2394 2899 2368 L 2899 2330 Q 3021 2323 3171 2262 Q 3322 2202 3459 2080 Q 3597 1958 3686 1766 Q 3776 1574 3776 1293 Q 3776 928 3625 633 Q 3475 339 3216 169 Q 2957 0 2624 0 L 595 0 z\nM 1133 2074 L 1133 474 L 2458 474 Q 2688 474 2854 554 Q 3021 634 3110 787 Q 3200 941 3200 1165 L 3200 1382 Q 3200 1606 3110 1760 Q 3021 1914 2854 1994 Q 2688 2074 2458 2074 L 1133 2074 z\nM 1133 3994 L 1133 2534 L 2368 2534 Q 2579 2534 2729 2608 Q 2880 2682 2963 2819 Q 3046 2957 3046 3155 L 3046 3373 Q 3046 3571 2963 3708 Q 2880 3846 2729 3920 Q 2579 3994 2368 3994 L 1133 3994 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/>