173 1818 0 L 1126 0 Q 1606 352 1945 685 Q 2285 1018 2509 1408 Q 2733 1798 2854 2317 L 2822 2330 Q 2720 2150 2573 2003 Q 2426 1856 2224 1773 Q 2022 1690 1747 1690 Q 1363 1690 1065 1856 Q 768 2022 598 2332 Q 429 2643 429 3066 Q 429 3507 614 3840 Q 800 4173 1133 4358 Q 1466 4544 1914 4544 Q 2381 4544 2713 4336 Q 3046 4128 3228 3744 Q 3411 3360 3411 2829 z\nM 1920 2144 Q 2214 2144 2422 2253 Q 2630 2362 2742 2573 Q 2854 2784 2854 3085 L 2854 3136 Q 2854 3437 2742 3648 Q 2630 3859 2422 3968 Q 2214 4077 1920 4077 Q 1626 4077 1418 3968 Q 1210 3859 1098 3648 Q 986 3437 986 3136 L 986 3085 Q 986 2784 1098 2573 Q 1210 2362 1418 2253 Q 1626 2144 1920 2144 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-8f\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-43\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_15\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(258.063417 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-8f\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3f\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_16\"><g style=\"fill: #2d3748\" transform=\"translate(326.434958 15.4) scale(0.08 -0.08)\"><defs><path id=\"IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" d=\"M 1926 -77 Q 1466 -77 1130 131 Q 794 339 611 723 Q 429 1107 429 1638 Q 429 2138 573 2573 Q 717 3008 957 3373 Q 1197 3738 1475 4016 Q 1754 4294 2022 4467 L 2714 4467 Q 2240 4122 1897 3786 Q 1555 3450 1331 3059 Q 1107 2669 986 2150 L 1018 2138 Q 1126 2323 1270 2467 Q 1414 2611 1619 2694 Q 1824 2778 2093 2778 Q 2477 2778 2774 2611 Q 3072 2445 3241 2134 Q 3411 1824 3411 1402 Q 3411 966 3225 630 Q 3040 294 2707 108 Q 2374 -77 1926 -77 z\nM 1920 390 Q 2214 390 2422 499 Q 2630 608 2742 819 Q 2854 1030 2854 1331 L 2854 1382 Q 2854 1683 2742 1894 Q 2630 2106 2422 2214 Q 2214 2323 1920 2323 Q 1626 2323 1418 2214 Q 1210 2106 1098 1894 Q 986 1683 986 1382 L 986 1331 Q 986 1030 1098 819 Q 1210 608 1418 499 Q 1626 390 1920 390 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/></defs><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-40\" transform=\"translate(60 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5a\" transform=\"translate(120 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3c\" transform=\"translate(147.203125 0)\"/></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"pedff8dfd4b\"><rect x=\"25\" y=\"10.472\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"149.688\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · EBITDA bridge ($M)","note":null},"answer":"<p><b>Fill to 80%:</b> +60 students × $2,400 = +$144k per school; × 40 = <b>+$5.76M</b>.</p> <p><b>Fees +5%:</b> $150 more × 480 students = +$72k per school; × 40 = <b>+$2.88M</b>.</p> <p><b>10 new schools</b> at mature economics ($524k each): <b>+$5.24M</b>, needing $20M of capital.</p> <p>Year-5 EBITDA: <b>$26.2M</b>, about 2.1× today.</p>","note":"Fixed costs mean a 14% rise in students lifts school profit by 47%."},{"q":"What return would the fund make?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Entry: 9 × $12.3M = $111M; debt $49M; equity <b>$62M</b>.</p> <p>Exit at 9×: $236M; less $30M debt: $206M. Return: <b>3.3×</b> (about 27% a year).</p>"},{"q":"Which lever would you trust least, and why?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p><b>New schools</b>: they take time to fill, need good sites and teachers, and use cash. The plan assumes they're mature by year 5. <b>Fees</b> are the easiest to deliver but must be backed by visible quality, or families will switch. <b>Filling schools</b> is the biggest lever and fully in management's control, so start there.</p>"}],"reco":"Back the deal. Banyan earns $12.3M EBITDA today; filling schools from 70% to 80% adds $5.8M, a 5% fee rise adds $2.9M, and 10 new schools add $5.2M, taking EBITDA to about $26M in five years and the fund's return to about 3.3×. Filling existing schools is the biggest and most controllable lever, so put the first 100 days there. Risk: new schools may fill more slowly than planned. Next step: rank schools by utilisation and test marketing in the five emptiest.","great":["Builds school-level economics before company totals","Separates the levers in an EBITDA bridge","Explains operating leverage from fixed costs","Judges which lever is most reliable"],"id":69,"slug":"banyan-language-schools"}